WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.900
In 1930, an 18-year-old Scottish woman, her name was Mary Ann McLeod.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.180
She boarded the SS Transylvania. It was bound for New York.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.700
She came from the remote island of Lewis.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.480
It was a really rugged place shaped by hard weather and hard labor and limited opportunity.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.800
And like millions before here, she came to America searching for something better.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.180
Her sister had already come.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.700
And so when she arrived, she arrived with $50 in her pocket.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.980
She registered as a domestic.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.160
She was a nanny and a maid, a servant.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.360
And she lived that life through the depths of the Depression.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.500
And she slowly built herself a life here in New York City.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.300
Years later, she married a man named Frederick.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.380
He was the son of the German immigrants.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.560
They had first entered through America through Castle Garden.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.180
Remember I told you his name was Friedrich at first.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.800
Well, they got married and they raised five children in Queens.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.240
And eventually, they had one of those children they named Donald.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.660
He would be the one that would inherit eventually the family business.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:19.400
But he had an appetite for risk and a willingness to think and bet big.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.300
Lose big sometimes, but bet big and dream big.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.500
And to pursue something even larger than the New York skyline itself.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.800
But before becoming president of the United States, Donald Trump had a lot of work to do.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:39.480
He cut his teeth in real estate just past this wall in New York.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.580
And one purchase in particular, he called it his Mona Lisa, if you will.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.840
And it exemplifies his willingness to just take the bull by the horns.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.900
The building is at the heart of a lawsuit designed to ruin him.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.240
The address is 40 Wall Street.
